  m_Text: "Max Size: 90 mm\nSpecies name: Olenoides serratus\n\nTrilobites were among
    the most common fossil type found in the Burgess shale and around the world dating
    back to the Cambrian Era. \n\nThey were some of the most successful organisms
    that lived during this time period.\nThey are now extinct."
